# FastAPI + SQLite (SQLModel) ingestion pipeline

Always apply these rules when changing this repository.

## Async Python

- Use `async def` for all I/O (HTTP, SQLite, FastAPI routes, scheduler).
- Do not add blocking I/O in the event loop. If a client is sync-only, wrap with `asyncio.to_thread`.
- Prefer `httpx.AsyncClient` for outbound HTTP.
- Use SQLModel via `DatabaseClient` in `db/client.py` (local `pipeline.db`).

## Pydantic / SQLModel

- Pydantic v2 only: `model_config`, `Field`, `ValidationError`.
- Strict models at API/external boundaries (`JsonPlaceholderPost`, insert DTOs).
- Tables live as SQLModel classes `RawIngestion` and `ProcessedMetrics` in `db/models.py`.
- No untyped `dict` leaking across service/DB/API layers. Parse into models first.
- Settings live in `core/config.py` via `pydantic-settings.BaseSettings`.

## Layout

Keep modules in:

- `api/` — HTTP routes and response wiring
- `core/` — config, errors, scheduler
- `db/` — SQLite client, SQLModel tables, Pydantic API models
- `services/` — ingestion, processor, pipeline, plugin registry, `services/sources/`
- `tests/` — pytest + pytest-asyncio

Do not dump business logic into `main.py`. Do not add Supabase or any external database.

## Errors

- Raise typed exceptions from `core/errors.py` (`AppError` subclasses).
- Register handlers on the FastAPI app; routes should not catch-and-return ad-hoc JSON for those errors.
- Log failures with `logging` (no bare `print` for errors).

## Quality

- No placeholders, TODOs, or `pass`-only production stubs.
- Type hints on public functions.
- Tests must use in-memory SQLite (`sqlite:///:memory:`) and mock the external posts API (HTTPX).
- Never write test data into the local `pipeline.db` file.
